I really should have.

1562
00:55:58.090 --> 00:55:58.510
All right.

1563
00:55:58.730 --> 00:56:02.130
This episode ends with Michael coming out of his office.

1564
00:56:02.150 --> 00:56:06.950
He's successfully hidden in his office until 5 p.m., after 5 p.m.

1565
00:56:07.370 --> 00:56:14.190
And the entire office is waiting to confront him, both about the horrible health care plan

1566
00:56:14.190 --> 00:56:18.370
that Dwight picked, and to finally find out, please, what is the surprise?

1567
00:56:18.510 --> 00:56:18.630
Yes.

1568
00:56:18.630 --> 00:56:22.590
Because he's come in attempting to surprise us with ice cream sandwiches.

1569
00:56:22.590 --> 00:56:25.210
Oh, he about hit me in the head with an ice cream sandwich.

1570
00:56:25.530 --> 00:56:31.750
I mean, Steve actually, like, the look on his face after that take, he was like,

1571
00:56:31.830 --> 00:56:33.070
Ange, how close did that come?

1572
00:56:33.110 --> 00:56:35.230
I was like, Steve, you pretty much almost hit me in the head with it.

1573
00:56:35.370 --> 00:56:38.730
And he also announced so proudly, Operation Surprise.

1574
00:56:39.210 --> 00:56:39.610
Yes.

1575
00:56:39.610 --> 00:56:41.750
And so we're like, okay, what is it?

1576
00:56:41.870 --> 00:56:42.570
What is it?

1577
00:56:42.670 --> 00:56:46.510
And it's all he could come up with in his whole day was ice cream sandwiches.

1578
00:56:46.570 --> 00:56:47.590
So now it's the end.

1579
00:56:47.670 --> 00:56:49.030
And then he says that's not the surprise.

1580
00:56:49.150 --> 00:56:51.650
It's surprising, but it is not the surprise.

1581
00:56:51.990 --> 00:56:54.750
So at the end of the episode, you confront him.

1582
00:56:54.830 --> 00:56:55.090
I do.

1583
00:56:55.230 --> 00:56:55.610
I love it.

1584
00:56:55.730 --> 00:56:59.450
I loved being the person that confronted him because Steve is so funny.

1585
00:56:59.470 --> 00:57:01.510
And he turned to me and he's like, yes, Angela.

1586
00:57:02.350 --> 00:57:04.570
Thank you for reminding me.

1587
00:57:04.730 --> 00:57:09.410
So you ask him, point blank, what is the surprise, Michael?

1588
00:57:09.610 --> 00:57:12.850
And then he says, the surprise is.

1589
00:57:13.850 --> 00:57:15.570
And then he short circuits.

1590
00:57:15.930 --> 00:57:17.730
He just stops talking.

1591
00:57:17.850 --> 00:57:21.870
He just stops talking and it just starts to have, like, upper lip sweat.

1592
00:57:22.050 --> 00:57:22.290
Yeah.

1593
00:57:22.430 --> 00:57:24.770
And we all are just looking at him.

1594
00:57:24.910 --> 00:57:26.390
It is so awkward.

1595
00:57:26.750 --> 00:57:27.810
It's so awkward.

1596
00:57:27.950 --> 00:57:35.010
And I remember when we did it, like, timing it out to that moment where we start to, like, slowly leave each person.

1597
00:57:35.130 --> 00:57:35.450
Yes.

1598
00:57:35.630 --> 00:57:37.350
And how long that felt.

1599
00:57:37.670 --> 00:57:38.130
Yes.

1600
00:57:38.290 --> 00:57:39.290
It felt so long.

1601
00:57:39.290 --> 00:57:41.350
It really did as we were standing there.

1602
00:57:41.490 --> 00:57:44.350
And they had choreographed the order in which we would leave.

1603
00:57:45.110 --> 00:57:46.670
And, of course, we did many takes.

1604
00:57:46.670 --> 00:57:48.830
So we would have to come back and reset.

1605
00:57:49.910 --> 00:57:53.770
And I remember thinking, are we going to leave this?

1606
00:57:53.890 --> 00:57:56.390
This is a giant pause with no dialogue.

1607
00:57:56.390 --> 00:57:56.790
I know.

1608
00:57:56.790 --> 00:57:57.810
Is this going to be able to stand?

1609
00:57:57.970 --> 00:58:00.470
Because that was not something you did on television shows.

1610
00:58:00.730 --> 00:58:07.350
In fact, on television shows, especially comedies, it was pretty traditional to have, like, set up, set up, joke.

1611
00:58:07.610 --> 00:58:08.550
Set up, set up, joke.

1612
00:58:09.030 --> 00:58:10.830
And this was, like, a whole different rhythm.

1613
00:58:11.370 --> 00:58:12.890
And so, yeah.

1614
00:58:12.910 --> 00:58:13.910
I remember this.

1615
00:58:13.990 --> 00:58:15.850
And I remember he just had to stand there.

1616
00:58:15.850 --> 00:58:17.250
Oh, it was so awkward.

1617
00:58:17.450 --> 00:58:19.550
And then when you watch it, it's so, like, cringey.

1618
00:58:19.710 --> 00:58:20.730
But it's perfect.

1619
00:58:20.890 --> 00:58:21.890
It's perfect.

1620
00:58:21.950 --> 00:58:22.610
It's so good.

1621
00:58:22.610 --> 00:58:28.070
And there's so many times, like, when I watch episodes of The Office where I'm like, how does Michael come back from that?

1622
00:58:28.310 --> 00:58:29.730
Like, I say that to myself.

1623
00:58:29.910 --> 00:58:33.610
Like, how does he come back the next day and be like, we all knew there was no surprise.

1624
00:58:33.830 --> 00:58:34.530
We all knew.

1625
00:58:34.650 --> 00:58:36.790
But, man, we made him suffer through that pause.

1626
